ication of artificial intelligence systems to improve large-scale simulations of natural and other phenomena; the study of applied mathematics, computer science, and statistics, including foundations of methods and systems of artificial intelligence, causal and statistical inference, and the development of algorithms for artificial intelligence systems; the analysis of existing large-scale datasets from science and engineering experiments and simulations, including energy simulations and other priorities at the Department as determined by the Secretary using artificial intelligence tools and techniques; the development of operation and control systems that enhance automated, intelligent decision making capabilities; the development of advanced computing hardware and computer architecture tailored to artificial intelligence systems, including the codesign of networks and computational hardware; the development of standardized datasets for emerging artificial intelligence research fields and applications, including methods for addressing data scarcity; and the development of trustworthy artificial intelligence systems, including algorithmic explainability; analytical methods for identifying and mitigating bias in artificial intelligence systems; and safety and robustness, including assurance, verification, validation, security, and control.","idx":109,"match_words":["carry","the program","subsection","the secretary","award","financial assistance","eligible","entity","carry","research","project","topic","include","the application","artificial intelligence","system","improve","scale","simulation","other","study","computer science","include","foundation","method","system","artificial","intelligence","statistical inference","the development","artificial","intelligence","system","the analysis","exist","scale","dataset","science","engineering","simulation","include","energy","simulation","other","priority","the department","determine","the secretary","use","artificial","int